# Walkthrough: CRM, API Access & SSO Implementation

This document covers the features implemented based on feature-analysis-dec2024.md.

---

## 1. CRM Connection UI

**Purpose:** Allow users to connect CRM (HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive) from Embed Settings.

### Location
- **Settings → Embed Settings → CRM Integration** section

### Files Created/Modified
- [AgentCRMConnector.tsx](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/src/components/AgentCRMConnector.tsx) - New component
- [EmbedSettings.tsx](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/src/pages/settings/EmbedSettings.tsx) - Added CRM section
- [agents.js:232-264](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/server/agents.js#L232-L264) - Generic `save_to_crm` tool
- [agents.js:494-580](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/server/agents.js#L494-L580) - Multi-CRM handler

### How It Works
1. User sees CRM cards (HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive)
2. Clicking "Connect" initiates Composio OAuth
3. Once connected, agent has `save_to_crm` tool available
4. Agent's system prompt includes CRM capability awareness

### Testing
1. Go to `/settings/embed`
2. Select an agent
3. Scroll to "CRM Integration"
4. Click "Connect" on HubSpot
5. Complete OAuth flow
6. Chat with agent and capture a lead

---

## 2. API Access (Business Tier)

**Purpose:** REST API for programmatic content generation.

### Endpoints
| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Description |
|--------|----------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/v1/tools` | None | List available tools |
| POST | `/api/v1/generate` | Bearer token | Generate content |

### Files Created/Modified
- [api/v1/generate.ts](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/api/v1/generate.ts) - Generate endpoint
- [api/v1/tools.ts](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/api/v1/tools.ts) - Tools list
- [server/index.js:5239-5370](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/server/index.js#L5239-L5370) - Express routes
- [sql/SQL57_api_usage_logs.sql](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/sql/SQL57_api_usage_logs.sql) - Usage logging

### Rate Limits
- 100 requests/minute
- 10,000 requests/day

### Testing
```bash
# List tools (no auth)
curl http://localhost:8787/api/v1/tools

# Generate (requires Business tier)
curl -X POST http://localhost:8787/api/v1/generate \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"tool": "email_subject", "inputs": {"topic": "Product launch"}}'
```

---

## 3. SSO/SAML (WorkOS)

**Purpose:** Enterprise single sign-on for organizations.

### Location
- **Settings → SSO Settings** (`/settings/sso`)

### Files Created
- [server/lib/workos.js](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/server/lib/workos.js) - WorkOS SDK integration
- [SSOSettings.tsx](file:///Users/shahidhasan/createHalal/write-ai/write-verse-hub/src/pages/settings/SSOSettings.tsx) - Configuration UI

### Setup Required
1. Create WorkOS account at [workos.com](https://workos.com)
2. Add to `.env`:
   ```
   WORKOS_API_KEY=sk_xxxxx
   WORKOS_CLIENT_ID=client_xxxxx
   ```
3. Create organization in WorkOS dashboard
4. Configure identity provider (Okta, Azure AD, etc.)
5. Copy Organization ID to Settings → SSO Settings

### Testing
1. Go to `/settings/sso`
2. Enter WorkOS Organization ID
3. Add allowed email domains
4. Save configuration
5. Log out and sign in via SSO

---

## Environment Variables Summary

| Variable | Feature | Required |
|----------|---------|----------|
| `COMPOSIO_API_KEY` | CRM Integration | ✅ |
| `WORKOS_API_KEY` | SSO | Only for Enterprise |
| `WORKOS_CLIENT_ID` | SSO | Only for Enterprise |

